    ['Moment of inertia of solid sphere','I=\\dfrac25MR^2', ['\\dfrac23MR²','\\dfrac12MR²','\\dfrac25MR'], 'Which is the moment of inertia of a uniform solid sphere about a diameter?','Integrating spherical shells gives 2MR²/5.','Uniform solid sphere.' ],
    ['Moment of inertia of spherical shell','I=\\dfrac23MR^2', ['\\dfrac25MR²','MR²','\\dfrac12MR²'], 'Which is the moment of inertia of a thin spherical shell about a diameter?','All mass lies at radius R; angular averaging gives 2/3.','Thin uniform spherical shell.' ],
    ['Young modulus from longitudinal wave speed','v=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{Y}{\\rho}}', ['\\sqrt{Y\\rho}','Y/\\rho','\\sqrt{\\rho/Y}'], 'Which is the speed of a longitudinal wave in a slender elastic rod?','Wave speed is square root of elastic modulus divided by density.','Longitudinal wave in a thin rod; not bulk sound speed in a 3D solid.' ],
    ['Bulk modulus and sound speed','v=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{B}{\\rho}}', ['\\sqrt{B\\rho}','B/\\rho','\\sqrt{\\rho/B}'], 'Which relation gives sound speed in a fluid?','Compressibility sets the restoring force and density sets inertia.','Small-amplitude adiabatic sound in a fluid; use appropriate adiabatic B.' ],
    ['Poiseuille flow','Q=\\dfrac{\\pi r^4\\Delta P}{8\\eta L}', ['\\dfrac{\\pi r^2\\Delta P}{8\\eta L}','\\dfrac{8\\eta L\\Delta P}{\\pi r^4}','\\dfrac{\\pi r^4\\Delta P}{4\\eta L}'], 'Which is the volume flow rate through a cylindrical capillary?','The fourth-power radius dependence is the key signature.','Steady laminar incompressible Newtonian flow in a cylindrical tube.' ],
    ['Stokes terminal velocity','v_t=\\dfrac{2r^2(\\rho_s-\\rho_f)g}{9\\eta}', ['\\dfrac{2r(\\rho_s-\\rho_f)g}{9\\eta}','\\dfrac{9\\eta}{2r^2(\\rho_s-\\rho_f)g}','\\dfrac{r^2(\\rho_s+\\rho_f)g}{9\\eta}'], 'Which is the terminal speed of a small sphere falling in a viscous fluid?','Balance effective weight with Stokes drag 6πηrv.','Low Reynolds number; spherical particle; no wall effects.' ],
    ['Capillary rise','h=\\dfrac{2T\\cos\\theta}{\\rho gr}', ['\\dfrac{T\\cos\\theta}{\\rho gr}','\\dfrac{2T\\sin\\theta}{\\rho gr}','\\dfrac{2T\\cos\\theta}{\\rho g r^2}'], 'Which formula gives capillary rise in a tube of radius r?','Vertical surface-tension force balances the liquid column weight.','Tube radius r; contact angle θ.' ],
    ['Thermal radiation net power','P=\\epsilon\\sigma A(T^4-T_0^4)', ['\\epsilon\\sigma A(T-T_0)^4','\\epsilon\\sigma A(T^4+T_0^4)','\\sigma A(T^4-T_0^4)/\\epsilon'], 'Which is the net Stefan–Boltzmann radiative power?','Emission minus absorption from surroundings.','Grey body in large surroundings at temperature T₀.' ],
    ['Adiabatic relation (ideal gas)','TV^{\\gamma-1}=\\text{constant}', ['TV^\\gamma=\\text{constant}','T^\\gamma V=\\text{constant}','T V^{1-\\gamma}=\\text{constant}'], 'Which is the temperature-volume relation for a reversible adiabatic ideal-gas process?','Combine PVγ=constant with PV=nRT.','Fixed amount of ideal gas; reversible adiabatic process.' ],
    ['Entropy change of ideal gas','\\Delta S=nC_V\\ln\\dfrac{T_2}{T_1}+nR\\ln\\dfrac{V_2}{V_1}', ['nC_P\\ln(T₂/T₁)+nR\\ln(V₂/V₁)','nC_V\\ln(V₁/V₂)+nR\\ln(V₂/V₁)','nR\\ln(T₂/T₁)+nC_V\\ln(V₂/V₁)'], 'Which expression gives ideal-gas entropy change using T and V?','Integrate dS=nCᵥdT/T+nR dV/V.','Ideal gas with constant heat capacity over the interval.' ],
    ['Carnot efficiency','\\eta=1-\\dfrac{T_C}{T_H}', ['1-T_H/T_C','(T_H-T_C)/(T_H+T_C)','T_C/T_H'], 'Which is the maximum efficiency of a heat engine operating between two reservoirs?','A reversible Carnot engine sets the upper bound.','Absolute temperatures; T_H>T_C.' ],
    ['Drift velocity and current density','\\vec J=nq\\vec v_d', ['\\vec J=nq/\\vec v_d','\\vec J=\\rho q\\vec v_d','\\vec J=n\\vec v_d/q'], 'Which microscopic relation connects current density and drift velocity?','Charge carriers crossing unit area per unit time give nqv_d.','n number density; q signed carrier charge.' ],
    ['Hall coefficient','R_H=\\dfrac{1}{nq}', ['nq','q/n','1/(nq^2)'], 'Which is the Hall coefficient in the single-carrier model?','The sign reveals the carrier charge sign.','One dominant carrier type.' ],
    ['Cyclotron frequency','\\omega_c=\\dfrac{|q|B}{m}', ['qB/(2\\pi m)','|q|B/(2m)','m/(|q|B)'], 'Which is the cyclotron angular frequency of a charged particle?','Lorentz force supplies centripetal acceleration.','Nonrelativistic particle; uniform magnetic field.' ],
    ['Magnetic dipole energy','U=-\\vec\\mu\\cdot\\vec B', ['U=\\vec\\mu\\times\\vec B','U=\\mu B\\sin\\theta','U=+\\vec\\mu\\cdot\\vec B'], 'Which expression gives the potential energy of a magnetic dipole?','Energy is minimum when the dipole aligns with the field.','Uniform magnetic field.' ],
    ['Displacement current','I_d=\\epsilon_0\\dfrac{d\\Phi_E}{dt}', ['\\epsilon_0\\Phi_E/t²','\\dfrac{1}{\\epsilon_0}\\dfrac{d\\Phi_E}{dt}','\\epsilon_0\\dfrac{dB}{dt}'], 'Which expression defines displacement current in vacuum?','It completes Ampère–Maxwell law for time-varying electric flux.','Vacuum; electric flux through chosen surface.' ],
    ['Poynting vector','\\vec S=\\dfrac1{\\mu_0}\\vec E\\times\\vec B', ['\\vec E\\cdot\\vec B/\\mu_0','\\mu_0\\vec E\\times\\vec B','\\vec B\\times\\vec E/\\mu_0'], 'Which vector gives electromagnetic energy flux density in vacuum?','Its direction is the direction of energy propagation.','SI units; vacuum.' ],
    ['Thin-film constructive reflection','2\\mu t\\cos r=(m+\\tfrac12)\\lambda', ['2μt cos r=mλ','2μt sin r=(m+1/2)λ','μt cos r=(m+1/2)λ'], 'Which condition gives constructive reflected interference for one phase reversal?','One phase reversal shifts the reflected condition by half a wavelength.','One of the two reflected rays undergoes π phase change.' ],
    ['Resolving power of telescope','\\theta_{min}=1.22\\dfrac{\\lambda}{D}', ['1.22D/λ','λ/(2D)','1.22λ/(2D)'], 'Which is the Rayleigh angular resolution for a circular aperture?','The first diffraction minimum sets the Rayleigh criterion.','Circular aperture diameter D; small angles.' ],
    ['Compton wavelength shift','\\Delta\\lambda=\\dfrac{h}{m_ec}(1-\\cos\\theta)', ['\\dfrac{h}{m_ec}(1+\\cos\\theta)','\\dfrac{h}{m_ec}\\sin\\theta','\\dfrac{h}{m_ec}(1-\\sin\\theta)'], 'Which formula gives the Compton wavelength shift?','Photon-electron scattering changes wavelength by an angle-dependent amount.','Scattering angle θ; electron initially at rest.' ]
